    <Axiom id="AX_USAGE_WAIVER_DISCIPLINE">
      `gennady yagni` flags an added/changed EXPORTED symbol with under 2 repo-wide production
      usages (tests and barrel re-exports never count; a private symbol is flagged only at zero
      usages — dead code) — a spec-level diff gate run once per group, inside the dispatched
      audit's `npx gennady sdd-verify --profile full`, never inside a phase's own
      `setup`/`code`/`test` gate and never as an orchestrator preflight. A finding routes to a `fix`
      dispatch on the ticket that OWNS the flagged entity. That worker either (a) removes the
      symbol, or (b) genuinely needs it — then adds `- **Usage Waiver:** <reason>` to its
      contract/surface entry (`DBC_PORT_FORMAT` / `DBC_ADAPTER_FORMAT` / `ENTITY_SURFACE_FORMAT`)
      AND logs `yagni <EntityName> ← <reason>` by writing that literal text with the file-write tool
      to `.claude/tmp/<task-id>-<phase-id>-log.txt`, then running
      `npx gennady sdd-log <owning-ticket> line --content-file .claude/tmp/<task-id>-<phase-id>-log.txt --phase <PhaseID>` —
      the label alone is not sufficient, the log line is what audit cross-checks
      (`AX_AUDIT_YAGNI_CROSSCHECK`). Cite an `<ACR>-DL-N` only when the reason IS a real Decision Log
      heading, else `gennady yagni` re-reports as `ERR_CLI_YAGNI_WAIVER_DECISION_MISSING`. Public
      API for a named external consumer uses the `(external: <consumer>)` variant — mandatory label,
      same rule. On a finding the tool prints the exact `- **Usage Waiver:**` block — paste it
      verbatim, never compose it from memory.
    </Axiom>

